  "//": "Third-party notices per module of the JVM reactor (libraries, Spring bindings and the host test kit alike). build-assets.mjs writes <module>/assets/NOTICE from these rows (the poms put it at META-INF/NOTICE). Each row: name, version, license (SPDX id), source (URL), textFile (repo-relative path to the licence text; left out for a row whose licence text ships beside the files it covers). Datum's own MIT licence needs no row. Licence texts live in integrations/jvm/scripts/notices/ (copied from the upstream releases, npm packages or Maven POMs; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). Reconciled with ./mvnw dependency:list (runtime scope). Rule: jars do not repackage dependencies, so a row is owed only for bundled assets and for direct non-Boot libraries a module names itself (Jackson 3, Endive, Jimfs and Guava, Bouncy Castle); transitive uses of the same library in sibling modules are covered by the module that carries the row. Datum-owned and Spring Boot managed artifacts carry no row. A row with kind \"dependency\" names a Maven dependency the jar declares and does not repackage; every other row names files the jar carries. Rows marked \"generated\" name the npm packages the shipped bundles carry and are written by packages/datum/scripts/notices.mjs from the bundles' licence files (npm run notices in packages/datum); the rest are hand-written. build-assets.mjs writes assets/NOTICE for every published module (a module without rows gets the header alone); the parent pom copies it and the repository LICENSE into META-INF.",
